  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MVI-Inclusive WG&amp;Climate Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Village (MVi), a Cambodian non-profit organization established in 2006 and officially registered in 2007. MVi operates in the northeast provinces of Cambodia, including Mondulkiri, Kratie, and Stung Treng. Its mission focuses on empowering Indigenous and localcommunities to manage natural resources and improve livelihoods. MVi emphasizes transparency, accountability, and community ownership while advocating for Indigenous Peoples&apos; rights and sustainable development. The proposed interventions of MVI for the implementation of IP3 encompass three interconnected pillars: Gender Equality, Disability, and Social Inclusion (GEDSI) and Feminist Influencing, Water Resource Governance (WRG), and Climate Resilient Communities. Pillar 1 aims to advance the leadership, agency, and representation of diverse women leaders, including Indigenous women, People with Disabilities, and marginalized social groups, to influenceWRG and climate resilience policies and practices. It serves as a flagship initiative that integrates with the other two pillars. Pillar 2 focuses on empowering civil society networks and coalitions to actively engage in WRG fora and policy processes, ensuring that diverse perspectives&#x2014;particularly those of youth, People with Disabilities, and Indigenous Peoples&#x2014;are included. Pillar 3 promotes resilience in riverine communities in the lower Mekong basin by addressing human and climate-driven changes through integrated community management approaches, such as climate-resilient livelihoods, disaster risk management, and sustainable freshwater and fisheries management. These interventions collectively address critical transboundary water resource governance issues and climate change impacts, including river diversions, hydropower infrastructure, changing flow regimes, water pollution, and habitat loss, with a strong focus on inclusivity, sustainability, and community empowerment for effective water governance and climate resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Village (MVi) was founded in November 2006 and officially registered with the Ministry of Interior in 25 January 2007. Ever since, MVi became a recognized local NGO working for Indigenous Peoples&apos; Rights and Natural Resources Management. MVi encourages ownership and participation of Indigenous Peoples# as its approaches to protect their land and natural resources.
MVi is operating in Northeast provinces of Cambodia, in particular in Mondulkiri, Kratie and Stung Treng, and focused on organizing community forests, helping indigenous people learn about their rights, helping women become empowered, and facilitating communities in undertaking various development projects.
MVi has been worked in collaboration with Community Networks, Provincial and National NGO networks, and line of government institutions at the national and provincial level of Department of Local Administrative of Ministry of Interior, Department of Forestry Administrative, Department of Agriculture, Department of Environment, Department of Land Use Management, and Department of Rural Development.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Village Organization</narrative>
